Backport of containerd commit 7a7aebfcbf6d3ce24d7b50eb2d7f9676b26c91d5
("pkg/oci: update TestOpenUserFileCapsReads to use newlined data",
Sebastiaan van Stijn, 2026-06-26), adapted to the 1.7 file layout
(oci/spec_opts_user_bounds_test.go, TestOpenBoundedUserFileCapsReads).

Test-only. containerd-1 bumps github.com/moby/sys/user to v0.4.1
(CVE-2026-61801), which caps a single passwd/group line at 1 MiB. The test's
padding was one 10 MiB line of NUL bytes, so it tripped that line cap
("bufio.Scanner: token too long") before reaching containerd's own 10 MiB
file-size cap, the thing the test is meant to check. Upstream made the
same change when containerd 2.x moved to moby/sys/user v0.4.1.

Upstream commit message:

    This test verifies the maximum file-size constraints that were added in
    [containerd7b05ec4]. However, github.com/moby/sys@v0.4.1 adds similar
    constraints, including a constraint on line-length (1M): [moby/sys@2c56c3d]
    that may hit before the file-size limit is reached if the data does not
    contain newlines.

    This patch updates the test to use data that includes newlines to make
    sure it's testing the file-size constraints, not line-limit constraints.

diff --git a/oci/spec_opts_user_bounds_test.go b/oci/spec_opts_user_bounds_test.go
index 7a0a58f..5025b96 100644
--- a/oci/spec_opts_user_bounds_test.go
+++ b/oci/spec_opts_user_bounds_test.go
@@ -65,7 +65,13 @@ func TestOpenBoundedUserFileCapsReads(t *testing.T) {
 			if err := os.MkdirAll(filepath.Join(root, "etc"), 0o755); err != nil {
 				t.Fatal(err)
 			}
-			data := append(bytes.Repeat([]byte{0}, tc.padBytes), beyond...)
+			pattern := []byte("# padding\n")
+			pad := bytes.Repeat(pattern, (tc.padBytes+len(pattern)-1)/len(pattern))[:tc.padBytes]
+			if len(pad) > 0 {
+				pad[len(pad)-1] = '\n'
+			}
+
+			data := append(pad, beyond...)
 			if err := os.WriteFile(filepath.Join(root, "etc", "group"), data, 0o644); err != nil {
 				t.Fatal(err)
 			}
